    "message": "chore: use the \\\\x00 escape instead of a raw NUL byte\n\nI used raw NUL separators in a lookup key. They are invisible in most editors\nand diffs — they render as a space — so the CI guard is the only thing that\nsees them, and it is there precisely because a raw NUL makes the file binary\nto grep/ripgrep, which then silently skips it.\n\nThe escape is the same byte at runtime, so behaviour and tests are unchanged.",
